the murderous robot with the killer  dance moves also known as Megan is  coming to a theater near you but can the  Android antagonist live up to all the  viral hype  Megan tells the story of a young girl  Katie who loses both of her parents in a  horrible accident she's adopted by her  aunt Gemma a woman who isn't quite  prepared to take on the responsibility  of a child let alone one who's been as  traumatized as Katie to help the young  girl cope with the loss of her family  and the repercussions of being isolated  at such a young age Gemma who earns her  living as a roboticist introduces her  niece to a project she's been working on  this project is a toy that can act as a  child's best friend a companion that's  supposed to chase away loneliness or any  other negative emotion Gemma calls this  toy model 3 generative Android AKA Megan  once the two are introduced to one  another Katie becomes very attached to  the eerily lifelike doll Megan seems to  be capable of Free Will so long as her  decisions are always in service to her  mission to protect Katie and ensure that  she's always happy however as Katie  grows more attached to Megan there are  concerns of her becoming too codependent  on the Android but when you've got an  advanced piece of Machinery like Megan  running around codependency is the least  of your concerns Megan becomes  increasingly aggressive in her pursuit  of caring for Katie ignoring commands  from the woman who created her and even  attacking a child she catches harassing  Katie Megan looks to be a growing  problem throughout the film with her  Fierce protectiveness spiraling into  outright murder setting up a showdown  between Katie Gemma and the killer doll  Megan set the world on fire with its  phenomenal trailer which dropped on  October 11 2022 attracting nearly 20  million views the Highlight moment of  the trailer where Megan shows off her  dancing abilities while pursuing her  prey even inspired all sorts of memes  while prompting fans to recreate the  killer robot's killer dance moves in  other words it seems the world has Megan  fever and we expect the film to make a  killing at the box office and yeah we  said box office unlike other films like  Halloween Inns which hit both peacock  and theater screens at the same time it  seems like Megan will exclusively be  playing on the big screen while the film  was originally scheduled for a January  13th release Megan will now dance its  way into theaters on January 6 2023  where it will no doubt Inspire even more  memes and hopefully just as many screams  in addition to all the free online  publicity created by Twitter and Tick  Tock users Megan has been getting plenty  of attention thanks to the titular care  characters online war of words but the  OG murder doll himself Chucky  hi I'm Jackie wanna play the former  Charles Lee Ray has had quite a lot to  say about Megan's existence but Megan  has done a pretty good job of clapping  back on Twitter having these characters  beef with one another as if they were  real entities has only added to the  Press revolving around the pair of  killer dolls and it's shining a light on  both Megan and sci-fi's TV show Chucky  when it comes to the character of Gemma  the filmmakers behind Megan decided to  cast someone who's no stranger to  frightening films the protagonist is  played by Alison Williams perhaps best  known to horror fans as the disturbing  manipulative milk-loving Rose from get  out she also starred in one of Netflix's  most upsetting movies the controversial  body horror film The Perfection needless  to say Gemma will be a far different  character from get out's Rose she  appears to be a loving but ill-equipped  aunt who's doing her best to help Katie  even if that does involve inadvertently  unleashing a murder Droid upon the world  as for poor Katie that part will be  played by the incredibly talented Violet  McGraw a young actor who has plenty of  horror experience herself she starred as  the young version of Nell in Mike  Flanagan's Netflix series The Haunting  of Hill House and she collaborated with  the director again in Dr sleep where she  played the young girl in the opening of  the film who falls prey to the vampiric  true knot Clan but who's playing the  titular killer dog all herself well the  role will go to two different actors  Jenna Davis will be voicing Megan and  you may know her from series like  Raven's home Scarlet's lab and Treehouse  detectives while Davis will be  delivering the lines Amy Donald will  actually play Megan the young actress  only has one credit to date she was in  Netflix's Sweet Tooth but she's a  talented dancer who was trained for the  role by Luke Hawker and Jed Brophy two  actors who specialize in playing creepy  creatures with strange movements  with the emergence of filmmakers like  Jordan peel and Zach Cragar there seems  to be a trend of comedians shifting  their talents over to horror it honestly  makes a lot of sense when you think  about it as horror author Joe R Lansdale  once put it I think that horror and  humor are opposite sides of the same  coin something that's really horrifying  is actually kind of humorous if you look  at it from a different angle and it's  the same in Reverse is that so yes  experts  when it comes to this trend of funny  filmmakers going in a scarier direction  we also have to bring up director Jared  Johnston The Man Behind Megan Johnston's  roots are in the world of New Zealand  comedy as he worked on TV shows like the  Jackie Brown diaries Terry Teo and the  new Legends of monkey however in 2014 he  began to get a bit spookier with his  first feature film The Horror comedy  housebound a film inspired by Ghost  Hunters where a dysfunctional family  must deal with the spirits inhabiting  their home Johnston earned quite a few  Award nominations for his work on  housebound from the likes of fangoria  freight meter and the South by Southwest  film festival with his movie winning  