es like Get Out The  Invisible Man split and long-running  series like The Purge Insidious and  paranormal activity with these two  powerhouses behind the film Megan is  already gearing up to be a wild ride  that has fans buzzing with excitement  when it comes to ratings quite a few  horror films boast the big bad are some  recent examples include slasher flick  Halloween ends the incredibly freaky  smile and Jordan Peel's sci-fi Adventure  nope however some of the scariest horror  movies of all time are rated PG-13 a  quiet place Drag Me to Hell and scary  stories to tell in the dark all carry  the more family-friendly rating and  they're all straight up nightmare fuel  blumhouse Productions also has quite a  few frightening PG-13 films such as  James Wan's Insidious and M Night  shyamalan's split and now it looks like  Megan is joining blumhouse's PG-13  Pantheon according to filmratings.com  the upcoming Robo Thriller earned the  rating for violent content and Terror  some strong language and a suggestive  reference as it looks like Megan is  going to go on a murder Rampage we're  assuming that's where the Violet content  and Terror come from and we're assuming  some frightened victim is going to drop  a few harsh words here and there of  course with a PG-13 rating well it might  not pack the gore of a Michael Myers  movie Megan is sure to draw in a wider  audience and earn those big box office  dollars  we know what you're thinking how can you  ask if there's going to be a Megan  sequel when the film hasn't even hit  theaters yet it does seem a strange  question on the surface but really it  shouldn't be all that surprising we live  in a world dominated by intellectual  property or IP where studios are always  on the lookout for the next big  franchise and it seems like the folks at  Universal think they've found one with  Megan it's honestly like she's part of  the family now while blumhouse is the  production company behind Megan  Universal is Distributing the horror  film in an article detailing the very  real possibility of Jason Blum and James  Wan combining their production companies  blumhouse and atomic monster into one  horror monolith the New York Times  reported Universal is so pleased with  how Megan turned out that it is already  talking about a Megan sequel Tick Tock  posts tagged Megan have been viewed 300  million times since the trailer was  released a month ago so it looks like a  Megan sequel might be in the pipeline  that leaves us to wonder will Megan  survived the original film will she kill  off the human protagonists or will she  be defeated and then rise from the grave  Chucky style we can't wait to find out  on January 6 2023  [Music]

